{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Help{% endblock %}

{% block description %}Searching, paying, baggage, refunds and travelling with children — what this site decides, what the fare decides, and what the airline decides.{% endblock %}

{# No `hero` block, unlike every article under it.

   The band is for a page with one subject: it names the thing you came for and
   the sheet rises into it. The hub has nine subjects and its job is to get out
   of the way of choosing one, so it takes the ordinary breadcrumb strip the
   layout draws and puts its own heading on the page background instead.
   ArticleHeroTest holds the articles to the band and this page to no band. #}
{% block content %}
<main role="main" class="help">
    <div class="container">
        {# A sentence and not the word "Help". The tab, the trail and the
           footer link all say Help already, so repeating it here as a heading
           spends the widest line on the page saying what the reader just
           clicked. The pill carries the qualifier the sentence would otherwise
           trail off into. #}
        <div class="help-intro">
            <h1 class="help-intro__title">Everything worth knowing</h1>
            <p class="help-intro__pill">about tickets and flying</p>
        </div>

        <div class="help-layout">
            {# The rail. Anchors rather than pages of their own: there are
               three groups and nine articles, so a page each would be three
               pages holding two or three links, and the reader would pay a
               page load to find out. `aria-current` is written by the script
               that watches which card is on screen; without it the rail is
               still a working table of contents. #}
            <nav class="help-rail" aria-labelledby="help-rail-title">
                <h2 class="help-rail__title" id="help-rail-title">On this page</h2>
                <ul class="help-rail__list">
                    {% for group in groups %}
                        <li>
                            <a class="help-rail__link js-help-rail-link" href="#{{ group.slug }}">{{ group.title }}</a>
                        </li>
                    {% endfor %}
                </ul>
            </nav>

            <div class="help-groups">
                {% for group in groups %}
                    {# `tabindex="-1"` so following a rail link moves focus here
                       and not just the scroll position: without it a keyboard
                       reader jumps the viewport and leaves the cursor at the
                       top of the page, and the next Tab goes back to the rail. #}
                    <section class="help-group" id="{{ group.slug }}" tabindex="-1"
                             aria-labelledby="{{ group.slug }}-title">
                        <div class="help-group__head">
                            <span class="help-group__icon help-group__icon--{{ group.accent }}">
                                <i class="fas {{ group.icon }}" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                            </span>
                            <div class="help-group__heading">
                                <h2 class="help-group__title" id="{{ group.slug }}-title">{{ group.title }}</h2>
                                <p class="help-group__summary">{{ group.summary }}</p>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        {# Titles and no summaries, which reverses what this page
                           used to do. The old hub gave each of five articles a
                           summary because there was nothing else to tell them
                           apart; the group and its sentence do that job now, and
                           nine summaries stacked in one column is a page nobody
                           reads to the bottom of. #}
                        <ul class="help-group__list">
                            {% for article in group.articles %}
                                <li class="help-group__item">
                                    <a class="help-group__link" href="{{ article.url }}">
                                        <span class="help-group__label">{{ article.title }}</span>
                                        <i class="fas fa-chevron-right help-group__chevron" aria-hidden="true"></i>
                                    </a>
                                </li>
                            {% endfor %}
                        </ul>
                    </section>
                {% endfor %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</main>
{% endblock %}
